From 7e32724a856e597a37175287e2538c5c060b9854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:01:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] [flutter_tools] Take the Linux host architecture from the
 Dart ABI, not uname

Class: upstreamable fix (backport). Upstream made the same change for
3.50 in #185369 (hostPlatform from Abi.current()) and #190480
(FLUTTER_HOST_ARCH); neither is in 3.41.9.

On Linux the tool ran `uname -m`, matched only `x86_64`, and called every
other answer arm64. On a ppc64le host that picks the linux-arm64
artifacts. Under a binary translator (qemu-user, FEX, POWERarm) `uname`
reports whichever machine the `uname` binary it finds belongs to, which
need not be the architecture of the VM that runs the tool.

Now:
* Linux, and other non-macOS POSIX hosts, map the name of the running
  VM's ABI (`Abi.current().toString()`, e.g. `linux_x64`) through
  `HostPlatform.fromAbiName`, and throw UnsupportedError for an ABI with
  no host platform instead of guessing arm64. The name is matched, not
  the Abi constant, so that an ABI the compiling SDK does not declare
  (Abi.linuxPpc64 exists only in the ppc64 SDK port) can still be mapped.
* `FLUTTER_HOST_ARCH=<x64|arm64|...>` overrides the architecture on every
  OS, through `HostPlatform.fromOsAndArch`, as in upstream 3.50.
  Unknown values are ignored.
* macOS keeps its sysctl probe and Windows its Abi check, now as
  `defaultHostPlatform`.
* `OperatingSystemUtils()` and `Cache.test()` take `currentAbiName` so
  tests can fake the host; the uname FakeCommands in os_test and
  cache_test become ABI names.

Tests: os_test.dart, cache_test.dart (99 pass, 2 skipped), on Dart
3.11.5 linux_arm64.
